            "review_title": "Review at Bai Duong Seafood",
            "review_text": "ajnarkin\nSan Francisco, California24 contributions\n3\nRude and Desperate!\nJun 2017 • Family\nStay away from this restaurant, folks. If you're visiting Nha Trang, you will probably go by taxi, and whatever you do, do not trust the taxi drivers for recommendations. They will give this restaurant to you as their first suggestion, because they are PAID to do so by Bai Duong Seafood. No matter what the drivers say, trust me - DO NOT listen to them and DO NOT go to this restaurant. \nFirst, there's bad service. One of the employees there was incredibly rude and ignorant. We asked the servers to send us seafood, and the chef ended up giving us this random dish that we didn't ask for. Then some girl who worked there came over and started screaming at US because they said we ordered the wrong dish. We explained that we had never ordered that dish in the first place, and the girl walked over to the chef and pointed and screamed at us. I have never seen such rude service from someone who didn't even manage or own the place. It was an overall humiliating experience. \nSecondly, to top it all off, it was amazingly expensive, and very loud in the restaurant. There were fans on everywhere in the restaurant besides from where we were sitting, and we requested for them to turn on the fans for us because it was BLAZING, and the employees refused. It was extremely loud and unpleasant. \nThe high price, the rude service, and the noise level - it's just not worth it for dirty food.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 25, 2017",
