            "review_title": "Review at Bai Duong Seafood",
            "review_text": "Companion395563\n216 contributions\n0\nPopular with the locals\nMay 2016 • Couples\nWe were walking and checking out the area as it was our first time in Nha Trang when we chanced upon Hai San Bai Duong (Bai Duong seafood). We noticed there were many locals eating at the restaurant so assumed it must be good. It was a large restaurant & about 75% of the tables were occupied by diners. We ordered grilled prawns(0.5kg) & clams(1kg). We ordered Saigon beers as well but were served room temperature beers. When I protested, the waiter brought ice. The grilled prawns tasted great but the grilled clams were ordinary as they were quite chewy. The place was visually unappealing but the locals seemed to like what the restaurant is offering. There was no menu available. You select the type of seafood you want to eat and then the boss will ask you how you want it cook. Unless you are going with a local it's best you seek a seafood restaurant with staff that can communicate in English. The meal cost VND561,000 including two Saigon beers.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 15, 2016",
